%% L2 — Orchestration and Control Plane: orchestrator-worker dispatch
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant K as Kong (L1)
    participant O as agent-orchestrator
    participant PG as Postgres (LangGraph checkpoints)
    participant M as memory-svc (L4)
    participant J as NATS JetStream
    participant KE as KEDA scaler
    participant W as agent-worker pool
    participant T as OTel Collector (L7)

    K->>O: POST /chat/stream (SSE upgrade)
    O->>PG: create LangGraph run, checkpoint v0
    O->>M: write plan as episode (Graphiti, via memory-svc)
    O->>T: span run.start (gen_ai.request.model=lead)

    par dispatch fan-out
        O->>J: publish agents.subtask.{sid} (subtask 1)
        O->>J: publish agents.subtask.{sid} (subtask 2)
        O->>J: publish agents.subtask.{sid} (subtask N)
    end

    J-->>KE: consumer lag observed
    KE->>W: scale up to match lag

    loop for each subtask
        J->>W: deliver subtask (MaxAckPending budget)
        W->>M: read context handle
        W->>W: execute (LLM call, optional tool call)
        W->>M: write result episode
        W->>J: publish agents.result.{sid}
        W->>T: span subtask (gen_ai.usage.input_tokens, output_tokens)
        W->>J: ack
    end

    O->>J: subscribe agents.result.{sid}
    J-->>O: results arrive (idempotency dedup at orchestrator)
    O->>PG: checkpoint v1..vN as results land
    O->>M: write reconciled answer episode
    O-->>K: SSE stream final response
    O->>T: span run.end (status=ok or partial)

    Note over O,J: At-least-once delivery; each subtask carries UUIDv7;<br/>orchestrator dedups by (run_id, subtask_id) in Redis.
